@{ ViewData["Title"]="Privacy and data use"; }
<div class="container py-5" id="main"><div class="card p-4 p-md-5" style="max-width:850px;margin:auto"><span class="eyebrow">YOUR INFORMATION</span><h1>Privacy and data use</h1><p>This page describes how this application handles your information. Digital Krushi Officer is an independent advisory application.</p><h2>Account and farm information</h2><p>Your account stores your name, email, phone, location, preferred language and farm details you provide. Passwords are stored as hashes. Email verification and password reset codes expire after ten minutes.</p><h2>Questions and crop photos</h2><p>Your questions, uploaded crop photos, responses and feedback are stored to support your advisory history. You, your assigned reviewing officer and administrators can access your query photos. Do not upload identity documents or other people's personal information.</p><h2>External services</h2><p>When configured, Google Gemini receives your submitted question and crop photo to answer your question and assess whether officer assistance is needed. Email messages use the configured SMTP provider. District names are sent to OpenWeather for forecasts. Browser voice recognition may use your browser vendor's speech service; review the transcript before sending it.</p><h2>Human review</h2><p>Routine AI answers appear immediately. Uncertain, complex or unavailable AI responses are routed to an active verified officer, preferring your assigned officer or district. Drafts for those escalated cases stay private until reviewed. If no officer is available, the case waits in the assignment queue. Published advice may still require local observation, testing and confirmation of applicable product labels. This application does not represent a government authority.</p><h2>Cookies and access</h2><p>Essential cookies keep you signed in and protect forms against forged requests. Administrators manage officer access. Signing out removes the authentication session from this browser; changing your password invalidates existing sign-ins.</p><h2>Retention and requests</h2><p>Records remain in this installation until its operator removes them. Contact the administrator who provided your account to request a correction, export or deletion. Before a public launch, the operator must publish its identity, support contact and retention schedule.</p><p><a href="/">Return to your workspace</a></p></div></div>
